Camoufox: Firefox Labs is off in a build without Normandy, with no policy file.

The new tab's Activity Stream starts only once Nimbus reports ready
(AboutNewTab.onBrowserReady). Stock starts Nimbus from Normandy, which this
build leaves out (MOZ_NORMANDY), so Nimbus counted as enabled (rollouts on,
Firefox Labs allowed) but never started. Every preloaded new tab's messages
then queued in AboutNewTabParent, each holding its closed window: the parent
grew ~7 MB per browser context and ~15 MB per crashed one
(tests/native/test_crash_recovery.py).

camoufox.cfg turns rollouts off (nimbus.rollouts.enabled). Firefox 159 reads
Labs only from enterprise policy (Services.policies.isAllowed("FirefoxLabs")),
and Camoufox ships no policy file, since any policy file puts Firefox in
enterprise mode (enterprise-policies.py). So Labs follows the build flag here:
with Normandy built out, Nimbus is disabled, reports ready at once, and
Activity Stream starts.

Guard: browser/tests/playwright/patches/nimbus-without-normandy.py.

